# Claim: a `Close` resource bound by an `if` pattern or a match arm from a temporary is closed when the branch or match ends, exactly as a plain binding of it is, and one the branch moves on to an owning parameter is closed once, by that owner, on o0, o1, o2 and with the checked allocator.
# Hand-derived: make(1)'s payload is bound, printed, and closed at the branch end ("closed 1"); make(2)'s payload moves into keep, which closes it when it returns ("closed 2" after "kept 2"), and the pattern's box no longer closes it; make(4)'s payload closes when its match ends; plain closes at run's end. Before the fix the pattern-held box only dropped, so "closed 1" and "closed 4" never printed.
fixture: PatternBoundResourceCloses.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0 # o0
stdout: = pattern_bound_resource_closes.out # o0
step: jet run -O1 main.jet
exit: 0 # o1
stdout: = pattern_bound_resource_closes.out # o1
step: jet run -O2 main.jet
exit: 0 # o2
stdout: = pattern_bound_resource_closes.out # o2
step: jet run --checked-alloc main.jet
exit: 0 # checked
stdout: = pattern_bound_resource_closes.out # checked
